    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "10 Salmon View Terrace, Sundays Well Avenue, Sundays Well, Cork T23H99H\nOM2 O'Mahony are delighted to present this property to the market, a beautifully presented two-bedroom period home occupying an enviable elevated position in the heart of Sunday's Well. Built in 1832 and thoughtfully architect- designed and upgraded, the property extends to approximately 74 sqm and combines the character of its period origins with a bright, contemporary interior.\nOne of the outstanding features of this home is its private gated entrance, south-facing garden and exceptional outlook across Cork City, with views towards St Finbarr's Cathedral and the surrounding cityscape. Internally, the house is equally impressive, with reclaimed timber flooring, handmade stained glass, an antique marble fireplace and bespoke glazed panelling among its many individual features. The result is a charming and comfortable city home with a distinctive character of its own.\n\nLocation:\nSalmon View Terrace enjoys a highly desirable elevated setting in Sunday's Well, one of Cork City's most established and sought-after residential areas. The property combines a peaceful residential setting with excellent accessibility to the city centre, while its elevated position affords superb views across Cork City.\nThe location is particularly convenient to UCC, Mercy University Hospital, Tyndall National Institute and the Mardyke, together with the wide range of shops, cafés, restaurants and amenities available throughout the city.\nThere is also an excellent selection of schools within close proximity. Nearby options include St Joseph's National Catholic School at approximately 0.4km, Cork Educate Together National School on Grattan Street 0.6km and Presentation Brothers College at approximately 0.4km, St Aloysius' School at approximately 0.7km, with other primary and secondary schools also within the wider locality, such as Strawberry Hill National School.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Composite front door; reclaimed timber floor; centre light, double doors with handmade stained-glass panels. \nLiving / Dining Room Southerly aspect; uninterrupted views; marble antique fireplace; reclaimed narrow beam solid oak floor; recessed lights; 2 radiators; 3 double power points; phone point; TV point; handmade timber panelled wall with custom made plate glass inserts to kitchen\nKitchen Porcelain tiled floor; modern kitchen units; fitted oven and microwave; gas hob; part tiled walls; ceiling lights; handmade timber panelled wall with custom made plate glass inserts to living room; glazed door and side panels to enclosed garden with shrubs.\nStairs and Landing Fully carpeted; radiator on landing\nBedroom 1 Carpet; radiator; panelled ceiling with recessed lights; walk in wardrobe with velux roof light; window seat; curtains\nBedroom 2 Carpet; fitted wardrobes; radiator; window seat; curtains\nBathroom Recently refurbished; fully tiled flooring; part tiled walls; white ware; large stand in power shower; radiator; medicine cabinet \n\nAdditional Details: \nBuilt in 1832\nNew Gas Boiler in 2021\nUnderfloor heating in bathroom\nGas Heating\nGas Hob\nElectric Built in Oven\nBuilt in Microwave\n\n\nDisclaimer: These particulars are issued by OM2 O'Mahony on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through this office. While every care has been taken in preparing the particulars, they are for guidance only and do not form part of any contract. Descriptions, dimensions, distances, references to condition and permissions are given in good faith but are not to be relied upon as statements or representations of fact. Purchasers should satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each statement. The vendor does not make or give, and neither OM2 O'Mahony nor any of its employees has authority to make or give, any representation or warranty in relation to the property.\n"
